# Tuesday.com — Task Management: environment configuration
#
# This is the ENTIRE configuration surface: one variable, no API keys.
# Verified against the codebase (src/lib reads only DATABASE_URL via
# Prisma's env(); NODE_ENV is framework-managed and never user-set).
#
# Setup:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   bun install
#   bun run db:push      # creates ./db/custom.db from prisma/schema.prisma
#   bun run db:seed      # demo account + 4 boards + 9 groups + 25 tasks
#   bun run dev          # http://localhost:3000
#
# Demo login (seeded, intentionally public): sepnetflix2023@outlook.com / Abcd1234

# ---- Database -------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite by default (zero-config local dev). The `db/` folder lives at the
# repo root, git-ignored. A RELATIVE `file:` URL is resolved against
# prisma/schema.prisma — exactly like the Prisma CLI — so `file:../db/custom.db`
# points at <repo>/db/custom.db for the CLI (migrate/seed), `next build`, and
# the running server alike, regardless of the process working directory.
# (src/lib/db-path.ts implements this resolution; tests/db-path.test.ts
# pins the contract.)
# For production, an ABSOLUTE path is still recommended — see
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §4.
# To use PostgreSQL:
#   1. Set provider = "postgresql" in prisma/schema.prisma
#   2. Set DATABASE_URL to a PostgreSQL connection string
#   3. bun run db:push && bun run db:seed
DATABASE_URL="file:../db/custom.db"
# PostgreSQL example:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/task_management
